    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "warm",
      "title": "",
      "uuid": "9f12098eccfa4a77a9ab9598212a9be6",
      "x": 4226.669866062293,
      "y": 4374.386032658736,
      "width": 300.0,
      "height": 424.0,
      "z_value": -9.740000000000144,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "body_text": "`BaseNode._prepare_for_removal()` is the single deterministic teardown hook. Every node subclass that adds **any** of the following must override it and clean up before calling `super()`:\n\n- `QTimer.timeout.connect()` \u2014 stop **and** disconnect\n- `QVariantAnimation.valueChanged.connect()` \u2014 stop **and** disconnect\n- `QGraphicsProxyWidget` \u2014 detach widget, reparent, `deleteLater()`, remove from scene\n- Background threads \u2014 set a cancellation flag **before** touching Qt objects\n- Any other signal connection added in the subclass\n\n`.stop()` alone is never sufficient \u2014 it does not sever the C++ signal reference and will cause a GC leak or a dangling-pointer crash.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "about",
      "title": "The Contract",
      "uuid": "bbfb9e9c83c64bdfb6284f6e5bd0bcf6",
