      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "about",
      "title": "Lifecycle",
      "uuid": "503d959088264752a8893f3833208956",
      "x": 6310.503323843655,
      "y": 4.365061837770611,
      "width": 118.0,
      "height": 52.0,
      "z_value": -9.78400000000012,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": false,
      "label": "Lifecycle",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "warm",
      "title": "",
      "uuid": "71fa0c7aabed4902bc349ae68765d3ae",
      "x": 6417.905306025531,
      "y": -238.01174050263114,
      "width": 300.0,
      "height": 216.0,
      "z_value": -9.78500000000012,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "body_text": "Each node has an EmojiButton in the top-left button strip. It renders a single emoji glyph from the shared pool, shuffles to a random one on click, and shuffles fresh on every session load. The graph never looks the same twice.\n\nThe emoji pool lives in `utils/IconPicker.py` \u2014 28 emoji in total, curated for warmth and personality."
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "about",
      "title": "Core Mechanism",
      "uuid": "2d502f3fd7bd46a69fef5e9f0fe6d37f",
      "x": 6600.783580119907,
      "y": -340.16140662134603,
      "width": 168.0,
      "height": 52.0,
      "z_value": -9.786000000000119,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": false,
      "label": "Core Mechanism",
      "depth_front": false,
      "node_tint": ""
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "warm",
      "title": "",
      "uuid": "66201b5a59ba42a4b078ce1cc8469e9e",
      "x": 12494.77470934819,
      "y": -684.6131254998959,
      "width": 300.0,
      "height": 248.0,
      "z_value": -9.789000000000117,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "shelf_visible": true,
      "body_text": "- The button is a `QGraphicsObject` child of the node, not part of the paint pipeline. It positions itself via `_position_buttons()` in the button strip.\n- `get_emoji` and `set_emoji` are lambda closures capturing `self.data.emoji`. The `detach()` method nulls these before removal to prevent GC reference cycles.\n- The shuffle uses `random.choice()` which gives uniform distribution across the 28-emoji pool. No weighting, no history \u2014 pure random, every click."
    },
    {
      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "about",
      "title": "Technical Notes",
